  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Consolidating CSS Styles**\n\nI\'m now integrating the custom styles, including `.bg-pattern`, `.wave-bar`, `.bento-card`, along with scrollbar and Material Symbol styles, into `src/index.css`. This ensures accurate and seamless rendering. I\'m also reviewing the design system tokens for colors, specifically the `primary` color: `#000666`.\n\n\n**Defining Design Tokens and Data**\n\nI\'ve outlined new design system tokens and integrated them, including deep navy, and associated colors like `on-primary` and `secondary`. Furthermore, I\'ve created the ambient background pattern specifications. Now, I\'m focusing on application structure. I am developing `src/types.ts` for interfaces and `src/data/mockData.ts` for rich initial data, incorporating data from the screenshots, such as \"Weekly Marketing Sync\" and \"Client Onboarding: TechCorp\" meeting data. I will include the avatars to represent data as accurately as possible.\n\n\n**Organizing Project Structure**\n\nI am now focusing on structuring the core application components. I\'m currently working on `Sidebar.tsx`, the side navigation with the MinuteFlow logo, \"New Minute\" button, navigation links, and a cloud sync indicator. Then, I will develop the top app bar component. I need a search bar with autocomplete, filters, a notifications bell with a dropdown drawer, and a user profile avatar. I\'m also preparing for the dashboard view that includes welcome banners and several bento cards. I need an upcoming schedule card, interactive action items with quick toggle and add functionalities, and recent minutes with status pills and attendee avatars.\n\n\n**Developing Library & Editor Views**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `LibraryView.tsx`, starting with the directory navigation sidebar and smart tag filters. Then I\'ll implement the view mode switcher and bulk selection actions. After that, I will work on the core minute cards, incorporating the 3-dot dropdown for actions like editing and deleting. Simultaneously, I am moving into the `MinuteEditorView.tsx`. The breadcrumb navigation is in progress. The Save Draft and Publish Minute buttons are up next, along with the left and right columns with detailed meeting and action item components. The floating dictation bar and voice transcription are top priorities as well.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 643084323
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
