  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Interface Elements**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focusing on the CSS updates required to fully implement this sleek interface theme. I\'ve pinpointed `src/index.css` as the main area of concern. Specifically, I\'m examining the base font and colors \342\200\223 considering `text-slate-800` and `bg-slate-50` \342\200\223 and I\'m looking at how to integrate a sleek slate background with a subtle dot matrix pattern under `.bg-pattern`.\n\n\n**Refining Component Styling**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the specifics, like the bento card style: a clean white background, a light border and subtle shadow. I\'m also looking at the scrollbar customization. I\'m aiming for the thumb to be `#cbd5e1` and hover as `#94a3b8`. Then I\'m moving on to the app layout, where I will define the background and text color, along with styles for the mobile navigation and sidebar component.\n\n\n**Defining Component Styles**\n\nI\'ve been working on styling the navigation items, differentiating between active and inactive states with appropriate colors and backgrounds. I\'ve defined styles for the footer and cloud sync badge. Now, I am turning my attention to the top app bar, where I will define the container style, the search input, the search dropdown, and the notification button, along with the user profile style. Finally, I\'m defining the page container for the dashboard view.\n\n\n**Defining Sleek Elements**\n\nI\'m now detailing some style elements. I\'ve considered the text styles for headers and subtitles, along with the button styles, including primary and secondary options. The schedule card and its items are now defined, along with their time tags. I\'ve also specified action item card styles, including checkboxes and badges for \"Due Today\" and \"Assigned\". Finally, I\'m working on metric and progress bar styles to match the Sleek Interface, and now I\'m working on the Recent Minutes section.\n\n\n**Specifying Visual Attributes**\n\nI\'m now detailing visual elements such as status pills, with colors like `emerald-700` for \"Approved\" and `indigo-700` for \"Draft.\" I\'m also styling the floating button, giving it an `indigo-600` background and a `shadow-indigo-200` shadow.\n\nIn the LibraryView, I\'m defining the background, the sidebar and tags, differentiating active folders with `indigo-50` and tags with varying colors. I\'m also finalizing the card and table styles with slate borders and white backgrounds. I\'m also now configuring MinuteEditorView, specifically the header with a frosted background, and the primary publish button with sleek effects.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 55947432
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
