  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Core Files**\n\nI\'m now diving into the code, starting with key files like `src/App.tsx`, `src/components/ExportShareModal.tsx`, `src/components/ContactPickerModal.tsx`, `src/components/SettingsView.tsx`, and `src/components/Toast.tsx`. I\'m also including `index.html` and `metadata.json` for context. The current plan involves analyzing `src/types.ts` to examine the statuses declared within.\n\n\n**Localizing into Spanish**\n\nI\'ve decided to proceed directly with natural Spanish for `MinuteStatus`, updating it to \'Borrador\', \'Aprobada\', \'Pendiente de firma\', and \'Finalizada\'. Now, I\'m focusing on localizing the key files. I am planning to translate `metadata.json`, `index.html` (including the `<html lang=\"es\">` tag, `<title>`, and `<meta>` tags), and, of course, the `MinuteStatus` enum within `src/types.ts`.\n\n\n**Examining Mock Data**\n\nI\'m now closely reviewing `src/data/mockData.ts`. I have begun to translate the attendee roles, schedule titles, participants, and action items. I am also working through the various directory names. The goal is to ensure the mock data reflects authentic Spanish terms and phrases, useful for testing the localized application.\n\n\n**Translating Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific UI elements. I\'m translating titles and dates within the mock list into natural, executive Spanish, including phrases like \"Ayer,\" \"Lun, 14,\" and \"Semana pasada.\" I\'m also addressing the sidebar elements in `src/components/Sidebar.tsx`, such as \"MinuteFlow,\" \"Suite Ejecutiva,\" the \"Nueva Acta\" button, and navigation options like \"Panel Principal\" and \"Biblioteca.\" I\'m then moving onto `src/components/TopAppBar.tsx`, where I\'m localizing the search placeholder, results messages, and notification texts.\n\n\n**Localizing Core Components**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in localizing key components. For the dashboard, I\'m working through translations for \"Bienvenida de nuevo, Sarah\", and various button and section labels like \"Todas las Actas\", \"Pr\303\263ximas Reuniones\", \"Tareas y Compromisos\". I\'m also addressing the calendar modal and the library view. The goal is to provide a complete Spanish interface. I\'m focusing on authentic and precise translations. I am also working through the mock data.\n\n\n**Translating Minute Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the components within the minute editor. I am translating interface elements such as \"Etiquetas Inteligentes\" for filtering, the bulk action bar (\"Seleccionar todo,\" etc.), the \"No se encontraron actas\" messages for empty states, and the various elements within the minute cards, like the three-dot menu, status labels, and attendee counts. I\'m also localizing the table list headers.\n\n\n\n**Localizing Minute Editor**\n\nI\'m now deep in the minute editor UI. I\'m localizing the right column elements, including \"Puntos Tratados\" with formatting options, and the \"Tareas y Compromisos (N)\" section with its various actions, placeholders, and buttons. I\'m also working on the voice dictation assistant and translating sample text and the visual feedback elements. I\'m then localizing `src/components/ExportShareModal.tsx`.\n\n\n\n**Refining Export & Sharing**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the export and sharing flow. Specifically, I\'m defining the email template in Spanish, incorporating fields for \"Para:\", \"Asunto,\" a greeting, and key content sections. I\'m also localizing the footer buttons, including the copy-to-clipboard functionality. Then, I am localizing the `ContactPickerModal` by addressing the \"Seleccionar Asistentes\" prompt, the placeholder text, and action buttons. Lastly, I\'m addressing strings in `SettingsView.tsx`.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 242925063
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
