    thinking: "**Defining User Profile Edits**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the user profile edit functionality. I\'ve broken down the \"necesito ahora cambiar el perfil del usuario\" request, identifying the key editable fields: Full Name, Role, Email, Department, Avatar, and Plan. I\'m thinking I\'ll integrate this in `SettingsView.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing Profile Edits**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in implementing the profile editing functionality. I\'ve designed an \"Editar Perfil\" button for the Executive Profile card, with either an inline editor or a modal. The `userProfile` state will live at the `App.tsx` level, persisting via `localStorage`, and I\'ll pass it down to `TopAppBar`, `DashboardView`, and `SettingsView`. I\'m even planning a quick \"Editar Perfil\" action directly from the `TopAppBar`\'s profile dropdown.\n\n\n**Adding New Assistants**\n\nI\'m now focused on adding new assistants within the contact picker. I envision a prominent form for \"+ Crear nuevo asistente\" with fields for name, role, email, and avatar. There will also be a toggle between the directory and the new assistant creation form. I plan to save new attendees to the `contacts` list in `App.tsx` and `localStorage`, automatically selecting them for the current meeting minutes. The assistant directory will also be accessible in `SettingsView.tsx` with management capabilities. I will add clear selection instructions in `MinuteEditorView.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 820049625
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
