  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Component Interfaces**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the interfaces for a new component, `ContactPickerModal.tsx`. I need to ensure it accepts an `isOpen` boolean, `onClose` function, the current and all contacts as `Attendee` arrays, and an `onToggleAttendee` function. This outlines the component\'s API for external control and data management.\n\n\n**Expanding Component Functionality**\n\nI\'ve expanded `ContactPickerModal.tsx` to include `onAddAttendee` (or `onAddAttendee: (attendee: Attendee) => void`) and `onCreateContact: (newContact: Attendee) => void` functions. Furthermore, I\'m integrating a custom directory attendee deletion via `onDeleteContact?: (id: string) => void`. Now, I\'m designing two tabs within the modal. One, a searchable directory; the other, a form to register and add a new contact with avatar options and save. I\'ve also added user contact removal.\n\n\n**Refining User Profile Features**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the \'Perfil Ejecutivo Editable\' feature. I have added `userProfile: UserProfile`, `onUpdateUserProfile: (updated: UserProfile) => void`, `allAttendees: Attendee[]`, `onCreateContact: (newContact: Attendee) => void`, `onDeleteContact: (id: string) => void`, and `onShowToast: (msg: string) => void` to handle user profile data, updates, contact management, and feedback. The plan includes an editable card with avatar, name, role, and other details, along with an \"Editar Perfil\" toggle.\n\n\n**Integrating User Profile Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user profile data across the application. `TopAppBar.tsx` will display the user\'s avatar, name, and role, while `DashboardView.tsx` will greet the user by name. I\'m storing `userProfile` and `allAttendees` within `App.tsx` using local storage for persistence. Moreover, I\'m integrating the `MinuteEditorView.tsx` with the `ContactPickerModal`, ensuring attendees are managed efficiently within the minute-taking workflow.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
