  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s need. I\'m dissecting the request for a calendar visualization on the dashboard. I\'m clarifying the requirement to integrate \"action items\" based on their \"due date\". The goal is to provide a calendar view that\'s functional and visually informative.\n\n\n**Developing the Visuals**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to make the calendar interactive and rich. An interactive calendar view, either full or mini, is the focal point. I\'m exploring toggle options between an agenda and a calendar view, or directly incorporating a dynamic calendar component into the dashboard. Within the calendar, action items will be displayed, mapped to due dates. This will include priority badges, completion checkmarks, assignee avatars, and due statuses. I\'m also planning to display scheduled meetings. Filtering capabilities will be important, too.\n\n\n**Refining the Interactions**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics of user interaction. I\'m focusing on filtering options, like showing all, pending, completed tasks, or meetings. Clicking a day should show its details in a pane. I\'m prioritizing direct task addition, completion toggling, and detail viewing/editing from the calendar itself. Navigation will be easy, using month controls. Visual indicators, like colored dots/badges, are also crucial.\n\n\n**Implementing Due Dates**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating due dates. I\'m ensuring all action items have valid date strings. I\'m adding `dueDate` and `priority` to the action item creation process within `MinuteEditorView.tsx` and `DashboardView.tsx`. I\'ve confirmed the `ActionItem` type already supports `dueDate`. Next, I\'ll create a dedicated calendar component, possibly called `ActionCalendarView.tsx` or `CalendarWidget.tsx`, to integrate into `DashboardView.tsx`.\n\n\n**Defining Calendar Features**\n\nI am now solidifying the calendar\'s key functionalities. I\'m prioritizing a month/week view switch, interactive day cells displaying task counts and badges, and a selected day inspector to show tasks and meetings. There will be an \"add task\" option on each day. I am also planning interactive filters, synchronization indicators, and navigation controls. I will focus on integrating these features directly into the dashboard.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 268278246
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
