    thinking: "**Designing the Calendar Component**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `/src/components/DashboardCalendar.tsx` file. The focus is on building an interactive calendar, specifically with navigational features. Currently, the design includes toggling between month, week, or schedule/list views to provide a flexible user experience.\n\n\n**Refining the Calendar View**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the monthly grid view. I\'m ensuring the calendar displays the correct days for any given month and year. I\'ve also added the functionality to highlight today\'s date and the selected date. Now I\'m focused on displaying meeting badges and action item chips within each day, complete with interactive checkboxes, priority indicators, and assignee avatars. A \"+N more\" indicator is also being implemented.\n\n\n**Implementing Day Detail Inspector**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the \"Day Detail Inspector.\" Upon selecting a date, I\'m designing the inspector to present a formatted date title, a comprehensive list of action items complete with completion toggles, priority indicators, and assignee details, and the scheduled meetings for the selected date. I\'m building an inline form to quickly add new tasks to that day.\n\n\n"
